  "narrative_insights": {
    "revenue_commentary": "Group Revenue increased 4.1% to €354.8k for the six months ended 31 December 2025, up from €340.9k in the comparable period [p.1]. The consolidated turnover for the period was €354,813 compared with €340,931 in the prior year [p.5].",
    "cost_commentary": "Cost of sales for the six months ended 31 December 2025 was €64,861, down from €69,600 in the prior year [p.5]. Administrative expenses were €781,975 for the period, an increase from €677,908 in the previous year [p.5].",
    "strategic_milestones": "The Company completed the acquisition of Loamin Ltd., a UK‑based geospatial AI business, during the half‑year [p.3]. It raised €1.1 million in new equity funding and completed a Direct Listing on Euronext Access Dublin [p.1][p.3].",
    "pipeline_outlook": "Senus closed 10 commercial deals in the final two months of 2025 with an estimated combined value of approximately €425,000, and the overall pipeline remains strong with about €700,000 of deals closed across 21 enterprise customers and an additional €500,000 of open pipeline [p.1][p.3]. The Board expressed confidence in the outlook for the balance of FY2026 as the pipeline of financial institution clients continues to expand [p.3].",
